From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:07:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 034/202] [ae-patch] Add host-connect observers and a
 server-side resume of an interrupted session

A host restart (a deploy, an update, a crash) kills every runner it spawned,
and the host comes back with new runner ids. _on_runner_connect is keyed by
the old runner id, so a session that was mid-turn is never revisited: it stays
failed with runner_disconnected until someone clicks Resume, and Resume only
relaunches the runner without continuing the lost turn. Reid asked on
2026-10-13 for those sessions to resume by themselves.

This patch is the mechanism; which sessions to resume is decided by an
observer the AE layer registers (ae_omni_policies.auto_resume), so without
one nothing changes.

- omnigent/server/host_connect_observers.py (new): an observer registry run
  as a background task after a host tunnel registers (so a slow observer never
  holds the host handshake; errors are logged, never raised), and
  resume_interrupted_session, the retry_session recovery for a caller with no
  request, with resume_interrupted_turn set so the relaunched runner sends
  upstream's own "your runner was interrupted, continue" turn.
- app.py: on_host_connect gets its own callback that announces the host as
  before and then notifies the observers.
- _recover_retry_session and _ensure_runner_session_initialized pass
  resume_interrupted_turn through to the session initializer, which already
  accepts it for child restoration; it applies only when the runner was
  relaunched, never to a runner that is still connected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
